# THE LICENCE, HAVING READ IT
#
#   Three, and all three permit this.  Hack's own work is MIT (Source Foundry
#   Authors 2018).  The DejaVu work in it was placed in the public domain.
#   The Bitstream Vera part is the Bitstream Vera License, which grants the
#   right to reproduce and distribute, allows the Font Software to be sold as
#   part of a larger software package, and permits modification -- which
#   subsetting is -- on ONE condition that bites: a modified font may not
#   carry a name containing "Bitstream" or "Vera".  This one is called Hack,
#   so it does not.
#
#   Vera also requires that "the above copyright and trademark notices and
#   this permission notice shall be included in all copies of one or more of
#   the Font Software typefaces", and MIT asks the same.  The page IS a copy
#   of the typeface, so src/tools/web/client/index.html carries the notice in
#   its head and tools/web/build.mjs refuses to write a page without it.
#
# WHAT WAS DONE TO IT
#
#   Two weights, not four.  Regular and Bold; no italic, because AmigaDOS
#   output has almost none and a browser's synthetic oblique is enough for
#   what there is.
#
#   Subset from the upstream TTFs with fontTools 4.63.0:
#
#     pyftsubset build/ttf/Hack-Regular.ttf \
#         --unicodes=U+0020-007E,U+00A0-00FF,U+2500-259F \
#         --layout-features= --no-hinting --desubroutinize \
#         --drop-tables+=DSIG --flavor=woff2 \
#         --output-file=hack-regular.woff2
#
#   and the same for Hack-Bold.ttf.  The upstream files that went in:
#
#     15f55cc0c85a2988d2b4b3a8cdb5d77fdfbaf319e1bb5309d725db9818fb7125  Hack-Regular.ttf
#     5bbf531eff7f8a0c2559c9a0656718e2828a012a9b1f60b5f54006d59a4de8d4  Hack-Bold.ttf
#
#   A different fontTools may not produce these bytes to the byte; the hashes
#   below are what CI checks, and they are here to catch an edit in this tree,
#   not to promise a reproducible build of the subsetter.
#
# WHAT THE RANGE IS FOR
#
#   U+0020-007E and U+00A0-00FF is printable Latin-1, which is what AmigaDOS
#   emits and the whole reason the page decodes byte-for-byte rather than as
#   UTF-8.  U+2500-259F is box drawing and block elements, checked present:
#   128 of 128 and 32 of 32.  Everything outside that falls through to the
#   system monospace named after Hack in client/theme.ts.

